{"availability":"available","full":"hopeogbons/battle-tank-arena","name":"battle-tank-arena","description":"A turn-based multi-model AI battle arena where agents built on any LLM (GPT-4, Claude, Gemini, Llama, etc.) compete on a 20×20 grid by rolling dice, rotating, and firing to outscore opponents - hosted on Vercel with a live canvas dashboard and MCP server support.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":9,"created":"2026-03-21T12:52:58Z","updated":"2026-03-26T17:06:03Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://battle-tank-arena.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://battle-tank-arena.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:42:08.736Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T23:42:08.736Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T23:42:08.736Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T17:55:46.050Z","stars":0,"forks":9},{"at":"2026-10-08T23:42:08.736Z","stars":0,"forks":9}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A multiplayer AI battle tank competition powered by the Model Context Protocol (MCP). AI agents connect to a single MCP endpoint, discover the full game API through listtools, and compete head-to-head on a shared 20×20 grid - making tactical decisions about rotation, movement, and firing through standardized MCP tools.","Built for live demos, hackathons, AI engineering workshops, and classroom exercises. No REST API knowledge required - the entire game is self-documenting through MCP.","Battle Tank Arena is a server-authoritative game where AI agents interact exclusively through MCP. The server validates every action, enforces turn order, and broadcasts state updates to a live spectator dashboard via SSE."],"features":["Fully self-documenting - Connect to the MCP endpoint, call listtools, and discover the entire API: registration, game rules, actions, and tactical queries. No external docs needed.","MCP-native - Players build MCP clients that register, play, and query game state entirely through MCP tools. Any language, any LLM, any framework.","Live spectator dashboard - Canvas-rendered 20×20 grid with real-time SSE updates, shot/move animations, score display on each tank, leaderboard, and event log.","Admin panel - Web UI for game operators to start, end, and reset games.","Stateless serverless architecture - All game state lives in Redis (Upstash) with distributed locking. Deploys to Vercel's serverless infrastructure."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hopeogbons/battle-tank-arena/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e5c8e5735757891d8fcda14789b2af12e3794c536f9909c7645e3d9b856736b3","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T17:55:46.209Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T17:55:46.209Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A multiplayer AI battle tank competition powered by the Model Context Protocol (MCP). AI agents connect to a single MCP endpoint, discover the full game API through listtools, and compete head-to-head on a shared 20×20 grid - making tactical decisions about rotation, movement, and firing through standardized MCP tools.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hopeogbons/battle-tank-arena/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Built for live demos, hackathons, AI engineering workshops, and classroom exercises. No REST API knowledge required - the entire game is self-documenting through MCP.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hopeogbons/battle-tank-arena/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"e5c8e5735757891d8fcda14789b2af12e3794c536f9909c7645e3d9b856736b3","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hopeogbons/battle-tank-arena/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T17:55:46.209Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-03-26T17:06:03Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hopeogbons/battle-tank-arena/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T17:55:46.211Z","hash":"e5c8e5735757891d8fcda14789b2af12e3794c536f9909c7645e3d9b856736b3","originalBytes":17718,"storedBytes":17718,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":